"},{"text":"Interaction_DragView","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Interaction_DragView","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A centered layer follows a drag in any direction. Origami’s Drag Settings","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"provide momentum and rubber-band bounds; releasing near the origin sends the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"placed graph’s reset pulse.","type":"text"}]},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".origami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swami","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"Swami","kind":"symbol"}}}